---
/*
  POLARISER — /variants/polariser/
  ================================
  This is the "sharp, opinionated, contrarian" variant.
  Direct will be clean+structured, Substance will be quiet+publication-style.
  Polariser sits between them tonally but visually does what neither does:
  hard contrast, aggressive scale, one accent that does not blend.

  Design decisions (why):

  - LAYOUT / LAYOUT-LAYER:
    BaseLayout is intentionally NOT used. The mockup specifies a custom
    HEADER with its own link set ("The wrong diagnosis · Method · Work ·
    Teardown") that doesn't match the shared Nav. Importing BaseLayout
    would force the shared Nav on top, which would dilute the page's
    posture. We render the full <html> shell here instead, so the
    Polariser is fully self-contained. (Constraint #2 explicitly allows this.)

  - FONTS:
    Body / nav / UI: "Inter Tight" — same family as the rest of the repo
    in spirit, but the "Tight" cut is denser, slightly more confrontational,
    and reads like trade-press editorial.
    Display H1 + key statements: "Fraunces" — a contrasty serif with high
    optical weight at large sizes. Polariser writing benefits from a serif
    that "states" rather than "presents." Using a serif for the diagnostic
    H1 + a sans for the body argument is the visual equivalent of
    a named author signing the opinion.
    Mono accent (numbers, the "35%"): "JetBrains Mono" — keeps the
    operational definitions visually distinct from rhetoric.

  - PALETTE:
    Near-black on warm bone (#F4F1EA), with a single hot red accent
    (#D7301F). The bone-not-white background reads editorial, not blog.
    Red is used exactly twice: the H1 underline, and the single CTA.
    Nothing else gets the accent. That's the contrast budget.

  - MOTION:
    Subtle. Body / sections fade up on scroll via a local
    IntersectionObserver (we don't use the global one because we skipped
    BaseLayout). The H1 gets one deliberate flourish: the red underline
    sweeps left-to-right after the headline lands, like a redline edit.
    Honors prefers-reduced-motion.

  - COLUMN WIDTH:
    Body argument: 38rem (~ 640px) — tight reading column.
    H1: wider (max 18ch on desktop) so the statement breaks where it should.
    Header / footer: full width, no max-width chrome — feels like masthead, not card.

  - BLOCKS:
    1. Custom header (masthead bar, monospace nav)
    2. Hero (the diagnostic H1 + activation paragraph)
    3. Filter (the rejection paragraph — visually demoted, low-contrast)
    4. The Turn (the argument — left-rule like a pull-quote)
    5. Single CTA — large, red, alone on the page
    6. Quiet footer — single line, mono, no nav links beyond what the mockup gave

  - COPY:
    All mockup copy preserved verbatim. Nothing cut. Nothing added besides
    the inline parenthetical the mockup already authorized.
*/
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>The wrong diagnosis — First Action Fix</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Activation-by-day-7, not trial-to-paid. The diagnostic for sales-tech SaaS founders at Seed to early Series A."
    />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />

    <!-- Google Fonts: Fraunces (display serif), Inter Tight (UI sans), JetBrains Mono (numbers) -->
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,500;9..144,700;9..144,900&family=Inter+Tight:wght@400;500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@500;700&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
  </head>

  <body>

    <!-- ============================================================
         HEADER — custom masthead bar.
         The link set is the one given in the mockup, not the shared
         Nav. Mono type to read like a section header in a journal.
         "The wrong diagnosis" is treated as the active item because
         this page IS the entry point to that essay.
         ============================================================ -->
    <header class="masthead">
      <div class="masthead__inner">
        <a href="/" class="masthead__brand">First Action Fix</a>
        <nav class="masthead__nav" aria-label="Primary">
          <a href="#" class="masthead__link masthead__link--active">The wrong diagnosis</a>
          <a href="#" class="masthead__link">Method</a>
          <a href="#" class="masthead__link">Work</a>
          <a href="#" class="masthead__link">Teardown</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main>

      <!-- ============================================================
           HERO — the diagnostic statement.
           H1 is the load-bearing sentence. The red underline is the
           one piece of "marketing" on the whole page; everything else
           is reading.
           ============================================================ -->
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="col">
          <h1 class="hero__h1">
            <span class="hero__h1-text">Your trial-to-paid number isn't the metric.</span>
            <span class="hero__h1-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </h1>
          <div class="hero__body">
            <p>
              <strong class="lede">Activation-by-day-7</strong> is. The percentage of
              trial users who hit your defined activation event within their first
              week.
            </p>
            <p>
              For sales engagement tools, that's <em>"first sequence sent."</em>
              For prospecting tools, <em>"first verified list built."</em>
              For lead enrichment, <em>"first enrichment job completed."</em>
            </p>
            <p>
              If yours is below <span class="num">35%</span>, the trial-to-paid
              conversation is downstream of a different problem.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============================================================
           FILTER — qualification by rejection.
           Visually demoted: smaller type, muted color, left-aligned
           rule. The reader who isn't the audience is told so plainly
           and the visual weight tells them too.
           ============================================================ -->
      <section class="filter reveal">
        <div class="col">
          <div class="filter__inner">
            <p class="filter__label">Who this is for</p>
            <p>
              This site is for founders of <strong>sales-tech SaaS at Seed to
              early Series A</strong> who've already noticed that fixing
              activation looks different from fixing conversion.
            </p>
            <p>
              If you're still debating onboarding email subject lines, you're
              working on the wrong layer of the problem. The work here won't
              help.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============================================================
           THE TURN — the argument.
           This is the longest block. Body type bumps slightly larger
           than the filter section to mark that we are now reading.
           ============================================================ -->
      <section class="turn reveal">
        <div class="col">
          <p class="turn__marker">The mechanism</p>
          <div class="turn__body">
            <p>
              Most Seed-A founders staring at trial-to-paid dashboards reach for
              <strong>product changes</strong>. New onboarding tour. New pricing
              page. New welcome video.
            </p>
            <p>
              None of it works, because none of it touches the actual mechanism.
            </p>
            <p>
              The actual mechanism is that trial users arrive at full attentional
              capacity. They have nothing to give. Every additional thing the
              product asks of them — every tooltip, every walkthrough, every
              <em>"tip of the day"</em> email — pushes them further from
              activation, not closer.
            </p>
            <p>
              The intervention that works <strong>displaces existing behavior</strong>
              rather than adding new behavior. It runs outside the product, in
              their inbox, where they have time to engage at their own pace. It
              teaches them what they need to know before they need to know it.
              Then it responds when they hit the moments they were taught to
              expect.
            </p>
            <p class="turn__close">
              That's the entire mechanism. Two paired email systems doing the
              work the product alone can't reach.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============================================================
           SINGLE CTA — the only red thing past the H1 underline.
           Generous space above and below. The supporting line is mono
           and small, like a footnote, so it doesn't compete with the
           button.
           NOTE: destination is /the-wrong-diagnosis/ once that page is
           written. Placeholder href="#" for now per brief.
           ============================================================ -->
      <section class="cta reveal">
        <div class="col col--center">
          <!-- TODO: change href to "/the-wrong-diagnosis/" when essay ships -->
          <a href="#" class="cta__button">
            <span>Read the full diagnosis</span>
            <span class="cta__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
          <p class="cta__meta">
            2,400 words. Worth the time if you're reading this far.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============================================================
           QUIET FOOTER — single line, monospace.
           No icons, no social row, no newsletter signup. The mockup
           gave four items separated by middle dots; we honor that.
           ============================================================ -->
      <footer class="quiet">
        <div class="quiet__inner">
          <span>First Action Fix</span>
          <span class="quiet__sep" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
          <span>By Andrew Z.</span>
          <span class="quiet__sep" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
          <span>Poznań</span>
          <span class="quiet__sep" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
          <a href="#" class="quiet__link">Contact</a>
        </div>
      </footer>

    </main>

    <!-- Scoped IntersectionObserver — local so we don't depend on BaseLayout's. -->
    <script>
      (function () {
        const items = document.querySelectorAll('.reveal');
        if (!items.length) return;

        if (window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
          items.forEach((el) => el.classList.add('revealed'));
          return;
        }

        const io = new IntersectionObserver(
          (entries) => {
            entries.forEach((entry) => {
              if (entry.isIntersecting) {
                entry.target.classList.add('revealed');
                io.unobserve(entry.target);
              }
            });
          },
          { threshold: 0.18 }
        );

        items.forEach((el) => io.observe(el));
      })();
    </script>

  </body>
</html>

<style is:global>
  /* ============================================================
     POLARISER — scoped global styles.
     We're not using BaseLayout, so there's no shared CSS bleeding
     in here. is:global is used because we're styling raw <html>,
     <body>, and structural classes that wouldn't get hashed
     usefully anyway.
     ============================================================ */

  *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

  :root {
    --bone:       #F4F1EA;   /* warm off-white background */
    --bone-2:     #ECE7DC;   /* slightly deeper for the filter band */
    --ink:        #131211;   /* near-black, warm */
    --ink-soft:   #3A3733;
    --ink-mute:   #6E6862;
    --rule:       #1B1A18;
    --hairline:   rgba(19, 18, 17, 0.12);
    --red:        #D7301F;   /* the one accent */
    --red-deep:   #B42514;
  }

  html {
    font-size: 18px;
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
    text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
  }

  body {
    background: var(--bone);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: 'Inter Tight', 'Inter', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.55;
    min-height: 100vh;
  }

  a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }

  ::selection {
    background: var(--red);
    color: var(--bone);
  }

  /* ----- Reading column ------------------------------------- */
  .col {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 40rem;          /* ~ 640px reading column */
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .col--center { text-align: center; }

  /* ============================================================
     HEADER / MASTHEAD
     Mono type, hairline rule, no logo mark, just a wordmark.
     ============================================================ */
  .masthead {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    background: var(--bone);
  }
  .masthead__inner {
    max-width: 64rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 2rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .masthead__brand {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif;
    font-weight: 900;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .masthead__nav {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .masthead__link {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink-mute);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    padding-bottom: 0.15rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: color 0.18s, border-color 0.18s;
  }
  .masthead__link:hover { color: var(--ink); }
  .masthead__link--active {
    color: var(--ink);
    border-bottom-color: var(--red);
  }

  /* ============================================================
     HERO
     ============================================================ */
  .hero {
    padding: 6rem 0 4rem;
  }
  .hero__h1 {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif;
    font-weight: 900;
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6.2vw, 4.6rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    color: var(--ink);
    max-width: 18ch;
  }
  .hero__h1-text { display: inline; }

  /* The redline sweep — one deliberate animated detail. */
  .hero__h1-rule {
    display: block;
    height: 6px;
    background: var(--red);
    width: 100%;
    transform: scaleX(0);
    transform-origin: left center;
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    animation: rule-sweep 0.9s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1) 0.35s forwards;
  }

  @keyframes rule-sweep {
    from { transform: scaleX(0); }
    to   { transform: scaleX(1); }
  }

  .hero__body {
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
    max-width: 36rem;
  }
  .hero__body p {
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .hero__body p + p { margin-top: 1rem; }

  .lede { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 700; }
  .num {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: linear-gradient(transparent 60%, rgba(215, 48, 31, 0.22) 60%);
    padding: 0 0.15em;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     FILTER — visually demoted band
     ============================================================ */
  .filter {
    background: var(--bone-2);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding: 3rem 0;
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }
  .filter__inner {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--ink);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
  .filter__label {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--ink-mute);
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  .filter p {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .filter p + p { margin-top: 0.85rem; }
  .filter strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 700; }

  /* ============================================================
     THE TURN — the argument block
     ============================================================ */
  .turn {
    padding: 5rem 0 4rem;
  }
  .turn__marker {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--red);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .turn__body p {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.18rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .turn__body p + p { margin-top: 1.1rem; }
  .turn__body strong {
    font-weight: 700;
    background: linear-gradient(transparent 65%, rgba(215, 48, 31, 0.18) 65%);
    padding: 0 0.05em;
  }
  .turn__body em { font-style: italic; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .turn__close {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem !important;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     CTA
     ============================================================ */
  .cta {
    padding: 5rem 0 6rem;
  }
  .cta__button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    padding: 1.2rem 2.2rem;
    background: var(--red);
    color: var(--bone);
    font-family: 'Inter Tight', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    border: 2px solid var(--red);
    border-radius: 2px;             /* squared, not pill — Polariser is not friendly */
    transition: background 0.18s, color 0.18s, transform 0.18s;
  }
  .cta__button:hover {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--red);
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
  .cta__arrow {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-weight: 700;
    transition: transform 0.18s;
  }
  .cta__button:hover .cta__arrow { transform: translateX(3px); }
  .cta__meta {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--ink-mute);
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     QUIET FOOTER
     ============================================================ */
  .quiet {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
  }
  .quiet__inner {
    max-width: 64rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--ink-mute);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .quiet__sep { color: var(--hairline); }
  .quiet__link { color: var(--ink-mute); transition: color 0.18s; border-bottom: 1px solid transparent; }
  .quiet__link:hover { color: var(--red); border-bottom-color: var(--red); }

  /* ============================================================
     SCROLL REVEAL
     ============================================================ */
  .reveal {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(20px);
    transition: opacity 0.7s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1),
                transform 0.7s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
  }
  .reveal.revealed {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }

  /* ============================================================
     REDUCED MOTION
     ============================================================ */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .reveal, .reveal.revealed {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
      transition: none;
    }
    .hero__h1-rule {
      animation: none;
      transform: scaleX(1);
    }
  }

  /* ============================================================
     RESPONSIVE
     ============================================================ */
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .masthead__inner {
      gap: 0.75rem;
      padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem;
    }
    .masthead__nav { gap: 1rem; }
    .masthead__link { font-size: 0.7rem; }

    .hero { padding: 4rem 0 3rem; }
    .hero__h1 { max-width: 100%; }
    .hero__body p { font-size: 1.05rem; }
    .turn { padding: 3.5rem 0 3rem; }
    .turn__body p { font-size: 1.08rem; }
    .cta { padding: 3.5rem 0 4.5rem; }
    .cta__button { padding: 1rem 1.6rem; font-size: 1rem; }
  }
</style>
